On X96Max_P boards with aml_dt=sm1_ac213_4g every write to the 0xffe09000
glue block faults (USB_R1 at 0xffe09004 is the first reached), so skip the
whole glue sequence for a platform that opts in with
"amlogic,skip-glue-init". The PHYs are still initialised by their own driver
through the glue node's phy list, as vendor firmware does.

diff -ruN a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-meson-g12a.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-meson-g12a.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-meson-g12a.c	2026-11-19 22:19:17
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-meson-g12a.c	2026-11-19 22:19:24
@@ -408,6 +408,14 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Every write to this board's glue block faults; USB_R1 (0xffe09004 on
+	 * the GXL layout) is the first one reached. The PHYs are still set up by
+	 * their own driver through this node's phy list, as vendor firmware does.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(priv->dev->of_node, "amlogic,skip-glue-init"))
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = dwc3_meson_g12a_usb2_init(priv, mode);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
